  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Step 1 · Install Mantis 2\n",
        "\n",
        "Install Mantis 2 from the GitHub release tag. This also installs its forecasting dependencies."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Z1R0zoGZFpO_"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "QEpWA8nbEps5",
        "outputId": "00deef9f-7b78-43fc-e4b8-3b91663969fe"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "  Installing build dependencies ... \u001b[?25l\u001b[?25hdone\n",
            "  Getting requirements to build wheel ... \u001b[?25l\u001b[?25hdone\n",
            "  Preparing metadata (pyproject.toml) ... \u001b[?25l\u001b[?25hdone\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Install the Mantis package\n",
        "%pip install -q \"mantis[v2] @ git+https://github.com/carsondudley1/Mantis.git@mantis-v2.0.0\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Step 2 · Download the pretrained checkpoint\n",
        "\n",
        "Download the Mantis 2 configuration and weights from GitHub."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "sC_G_snNGDet"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Download the configuration and the model weights\n",
        "\n",
        "!wget -q -O config.json https://github.com/carsondudley1/Mantis/releases/download/mantis-v2.0.0/config.json\n",
        "!wget -q -O model.safetensors https://github.com/carsondudley1/Mantis/releases/download/mantis-v2.0.0/model.safetensors"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "RfMx6eKVE4-l"
      },
      "execution_count": 2,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Step 3 · Load the Michigan example data\n",
        "\n",
        "Load weekly COVID-19 deaths and hospitalizations for Michigan. The two series are aligned week by week, so we can use them together to generate forecasts."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "lb3wyf58GR8d"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "\n",
        "data_url = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/carsondudley1/Mantis/mantis-v2.0.0/data\"\n",
        "\n",
        "deaths_ts = pd.read_csv(f\"{data_url}/covid_deaths.csv\")[\"mi\"].to_numpy()\n",
        "hosp_ts = pd.read_csv(f\"{data_url}/covid_hospitalizations.csv\")[\"mi\"].to_numpy()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "H2_uoN2oFlc2"
      },
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Step 4 · Forecast deaths and hospitalizations together\n",
        "\n",
        "Use Mantis 2 to forecast weekly COVID-19 deaths and hospitalizations jointly. Each forecast uses only the data available at that point.\n",
        "\n",
        "Each forecast has shape `(2, 21, 16)`. The axes are **series, quantile, forecast week**. Deaths are the first series and hospitalizations are the second."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "UG0V8ynHIPI9"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from mantis.v2 import Mantis2\n",
        "\n",
        "model = Mantis2(\".\")\n",
        "start = len(deaths_ts)\n",
        "\n",
        "forecasts = model.predict(time_series=[deaths_ts[:start], hosp_ts[:start]])\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Forecast shape:\", forecasts[0].shape)  # (2, 21, 16)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "iDk4qxeqG2Bx",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 67,
          "referenced_widgets": [
            "b419344f5aea4711a372ee10fa301761",
            "1276889b5c3a48ebac772d17f248af00",
            "e244d9bf528c4d3e8c6c27aaf56b408d",
            "d3c2951e2e064a89a350deeffd1ea69a",
            "e2e87f1b35f24857bf86cf0682803be5",
            "f12f4dfe07e443d8995c06dc6b10a65c",
            "72f1ec2d2dba487da0451a8284f396d8",
